{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Change:** Add a spread-calibrated market leg to the GSE ensemble: fit logit(P(home win)) = beta_0 + beta_1*(de-vigged spread-implied probability) on 2010-2024 NFL games as the market leg alongside the efficiency/model leg, grid-search the market-vs-model weight on past seasons' log-loss walk-forward (re-tuned annually), and replicate the paper's skill-vs-luck season simulation under the engine's own probabilities to publish the 'even perfect probabilities only win X% of the time' figure for pick-product expectation-setting.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Change:** Unify GSE's rating stack on the structured log-odds view: refactor the existing Bradley-Terry/Elo implementations so the log-odds matrix L is explicit (P = sigma(L); base L = theta.1^T - 1.theta^T + h.1.1^T; gradient step d-ell/d-theta = (Y - p).dL/d-theta, eq. 14) with rank, antisymmetry, home term, and feature terms as composable options; adopt two-stage training for NFL Elo (Stage 1: batch MLE on a multi-season block with no fixed K; Stage 2: online per-game updates with tuned learning rate), keeping vanilla rank-2 + home advantage + small binary covariates (rookie QB, short rest); add the Skellam score-difference head as an auxiliary training objective (predict margin distribution, derive win prob from P(Y>0)) for paired-competition outcomes.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Change:** Add a draft-prospect evaluation lane modeled on the paper's logistic model tree (LMT) for identifying exceptional players: data = NFL draft prospects 2000-2025 (college production, combine + RAS, draft position); target = played >=1 NFL snap within 4 years; tree root-splits on draft position / dominator / RAS with logistic leaves. As honest baselining (BASELINE): this only counts if the model tree's SRC beats draft-order SRC by >=0.10 AND beats a global logistic regression by >=0.05 on 2019-2024 drafts -- if draft position alone subsumes the signal, the tree is theater and consensus wins. The GSE improvement goes beyond the paper with a hurdle model tree: keep the logistic tree for P(play>=1 game), then a per-leaf zero-truncated negative-binomial count model for games-given-participation, ranking by E[games] = P(play).E[games|play] -- testing whether the paper's probability-as- ...", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "by >= 20% relative to OLS at K=4 with T~=1000 injected games, AND the recovered (sigma-hat-underbar, sigma-hat-bar) bracket the injected (3,10) bounds within +-1.5 points.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Change:** Adopt the paper's CATE ingredient ranking as GSE's default causal recipe: for any binary treatment (short rest, turf, new play-caller) and outcome (EPA/play, win, injury): propensity forest + marginal-mean forest, then a model-based forest on E[Y|x,t] = m-hat(x) + tau(x)(t - pi-hat(x)) with simultaneous prognostic/predictive splits — minimum viable version = treatment-centering only (mob(W-hat)), which captured most of the gain under confounding; Poisson-forest likelihood for injury counts, interval-censored likelihood for games-missed with heaping.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Change:** Build an availability classifier from beat-reporter language: scrape beat-writer tweets/articles (Schefter, Rapoport, team beat writers) + NFL official injury-report text; label sentences with availability outcomes from subsequent injury reports (Out/Doubtful/Questionable/Active); fine-tune DeBERTa-v3-base on the sentence-classification task, 80/10/10 split by SEASON (not shuffled), target = P(player misses next game | news sentence); serve hourly over the beat-writer firehose - when P(miss) crosses 0.6 for a starter, emit an availability signal into the pick engine 15-60 min before books move - with a domain-specific 'injury-language' encoder via contrastive pretraining on paired sentences ('limited in practice' vs 'full participant'), distilled into a 30M-param model for sub-second live inference.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Change:** Replace Monte Carlo with exact fixed-bracket DP for the 14-team NFL playoff bracket: P(team advances past round r+1) = sum over possible opponents o of P(o reaches round r) * P(team beats o), byes carried forward with probability 1 - pragmatic v1: exact bracket DP applied to the current projected seeding each week, published alongside the existing Monte Carlo as a cross-check; recompute weekly and live (clamping completed games to probability 1); output per-team P(win division), P(make playoffs), P(first-round bye), P(reach divisional/SB), P(win Super Bowl) with zero simulation noise - plus exact enumeration of division-race outcomes (<=4 relevant games per division race: 2^4=16 to 3^4=81 combinations) for exact P(win division), and exact joint probabilities (P(Team A AND Team B both reach the Super Bowl)) for pricing correlated playoff futures.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Change:** Weight GSE's team-rating BT fits by game informativeness via tiered-margin BT: fit P(i beats j | m) = sigma(theta_i - theta_j - m) with margins m=1.0 for playoff games, 0.5 for late-season contender games, 0.1 for early-season games, so ratings separate more on high-information games; then learn the tier margins end-to-end constrained non-increasing.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Change:** Add a scorekeeper-bias debiasing preprocessing layer: replicate the paper's 'potential' construct (potential pressure = pass-rush snap with defender within X yards of QB at throw; potential drop = catchable target per charting), fit hierarchical logistic regression P(credited | potential) = logit-inverse(context features + crew/stadium random effects) for subjective labels (solo/assisted tackles, pressures/hits, drops, broken tackles) on nflverse 2019-2025 + charting, and feed debiased stats (e.g., crew-adjusted pressure rate) upstream to EPA and prop models.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Change:** Replace binned recalibration with a BILR monotone calibration map (logit P(win) = sum beta_m b_m(model_prob), fully monotone, B-spline order 4, ~9 bases on [0,1]) fit in Stan, emitting smooth calibration maps with 95% bands applied to all engine probabilities before publishing, plus monotone 4th-down conversion curves by yards-to-go and field zone.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Change:** Replicate the winning pattern on nflverse play-by-play (2000-2025) as the ball-by-ball analog: per-timestep output heads trained on full game sequences with shared input embedding + recurrent core (LSTM first, then GRU/Transformer), features (score differential, time remaining, down/distance/yardline, timeouts, pre-game spread, pre-play WP), targets live spread P(home cover) and total P(over) at each play, loss = mean BCE over all plays with the final spread/total outcome as label at every timestep; append pre-game spread/total to every play input and ablate it explicitly (the paper's +13% ablation analog).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Change:** Build the hierarchical logistic QB/team/coach decomposition: logit P(A beats B) = (theta_QB_A + theta_team_A + ...) - (theta_QB_B + ...), cross-classified random effects for QB, head coach, offensive/defensive units + seasonal form (Stan/numpyro on 2009-2025 nflverse); identification via QB team-changes and backup-QB starts; report variance shares (QB vs roster vs coach) with CIs; add the QB x team interaction the paper assumes away as a 'scheme-fit rating' for free-agency analysis; serve the counterfactual engine P(team X with QB Y beats team Z with QB W).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Change:** Replace heuristic fractional Kelly with risk-constrained Kelly (RCK): for each pick, engine gives win prob p-hat and decimal odds o, choose stake fraction b solving max E[log(1+b(X))] s.t. E[(1+bX)^{-lambda}] <= 1 with lambda = log-beta/log-alpha (e.g., alpha=0.7 tolerate 30% drawdown, beta=0.05); calibrate lambda on the picks DB so realized drawdown frequency matches beta; extend to slate vectors over simultaneous picks with the joint outcome distribution.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Change:** Replace the plug-in Kelly fraction with uncertainty-aware Emc sizing: for each bet, draw M samples of the true probability from the calibrated uncertainty distribution around the model price (Sigma estimated from the grouping-loss/temperature-scaling calibration residuals), maximize mean log-wealth over the samples, add the chance constraint P(true expected log return > 0) >= 1-alpha with alpha = 0.4 tuned on backtest -- first in the paper-trading harness.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Change:** Build NFL parametric PageRank from the TenisRank tennis template: 32 team nodes, edge loser->winner per game, W_edge = W_recency x W_situation x W_importance; NFL analogs: recency = exponential decay in weeks; 'surface' = dome/outdoor and turf/grass match/mismatch (real NFL splits); importance = playoff vs regular season, rest differential; tune with greedy coordinate search on 2015-2019 maximizing walk-forward hit rate; P(victory) mapping: logistic fit of win rate on rating difference -> direct moneyline-probability converter for the calibration lane; decision-tree variants by dome/outdoor x playoff; run the market test the thesis skipped: compare the rating-implied probabilities against closing moneylines (CLV-style).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Change:** Build an NFL margin-distribution model on the Skellam-regression template: data nflverse play-by-play + rosters 2015-2025; target = final score differential Z; fit Z ~ Skellam(lambda1, lambda2) with log-links on unit-strength differential covariates (offense EPA/play, defense EPA/play allowed, QB efficiency, pressure rate, kicking -- the NFL analog of the soccer lines); validate against the binned empirical margin distribution (expect and document misfit spikes at key numbers +/-3, +/-7). Outputs: full margin PMF -> P(home win), P(cover", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Gate:** Adopt if out-of-sample Brier < climatology by >=0.02 AND P(cover) calibration slope in [0.9, 1.1] with >=80% of bins within 2pp of y=x; reject (stay with engine Monte Carlo) otherwise. If the key-number spikes (+/-3, +/-7) break calibration, the gate fails and the mixture experiment becomes the required next step.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Change:** Two props wins: (1) receiver-conditional TD model for anytime-TD and receiving props: P(TD on play) = sum_t P(TD | targeted=t)*P(targeted=t) - train a target-distribution model (who gets targeted from pre-snap/matchup features) and a conditional TD model (given the target, from coverage/separation features), marginalize; same for first-down props; (2) pre-snap graph for the NGS lane: 22 nodes with NGS positions/velocities at snap, edges = offense/defense + assignment proximity, GATv2 predicting play outcome (run/pass, yards bucket, TD), with D2-style augmentation: mirror across field axis (with play-direction normalization) to double goal-line/red-zone samples - plus situation retrieval: nearest-neighbor search in the graph embedding space for matchup prep ('find me all 3rd-and-long blitz looks vs this protection').", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Change:** Build the LS rating engine with precision: per week, form N (Laplacian of games played) and S (score-differential sums); mu-hat=N^+S with sum-mu=0 constraint; publish team strengths WITH standard errors (sigma-hat^2=Q(mu-hat)/n, Var(mu-hat)=sigma-hat^2 N^+) - a GSE differentiator - plus pairwise z-tests for matchup content ('model says KC is better than BUF at 95% confidence, accounting for schedule connectivity'), rejecting the omit-home-covariate simplification for NFL, and an optimal-design lane: weekly 'highest-leverage games for rating precision' via A-optimality (reduction in trace(sigma^2 N^+) per unplayed game).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Change:** ZI-Skellam2 margin model: univariate NFL margin Z (home-away points) ~ ZI-Skellam2(mu, sigma^2, p) with mu_jk = alpha + beta_j + gamma_k (team home/away abilities from nflverse 2015-2025); push handling: interpret p as excess mass at Z == spread (recenter Z' = Z - spread per game) - this converts the ZI trick from 'draws' to 'pushes', directly pricing push probability into spread bets; bivariate half model: (1H diff, 2H diff) with Skellam2 marginals + Frank copula, team abilities shared vs half-specific; output: halftime-conditional P(win), P(cover), P(over) for the live-betting surface; season sim: 10,000 Monte Carlo replications of remaining schedule for playoff-probability content - plus quarter-by-quarter vine copula: extend to four quarters with a D-vine of Frank copulas, Skellam2 marginals, abilities allowed a linear 'fatigue/adjustment' trend across quarters, testing whe ...", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Change:** Replicate the EPAA pipeline for NBA props: cluster players by shot-region selection and accuracy profiles (hierarchical Multinomial/Binomial), compute expected points at fixed usage N-tilde, define player EPAA vs league-average posterior; convert to betting: EPAA posterior -> expected points distribution for tonight's game (usage-adjusted); edge = E[points] - prop line; post only if edge > 0 and 95% credible interval excludes the line (ties to the 0714/0716 abstention gates); extend to other prop types: rebound/assist region profiles (analogous regions = court zones) - plus fix the paper's top-100 restriction: fit the hierarchical model on ALL rotation players with partial pooling (small-sample players - the paper's excluded set - are exactly where Bayesian shrinkage adds most value and where prop lines are softest); make the 'average' baseline time-varying (rolling 4-week aver ...", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Change:** Adopt the bootstrap error-quantification protocol for GSE's possession-value / expected-points surfaces: simulate from the fitted model (>=500 replications), fit log(error) = c + alpha log K + beta log n, and only publish player ratings or prop prices from the surface if P(error < threshold) >= 0.90; otherwise coarsen the grid.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Change:** Build a rest-of-game live model from the paper's in-game random walk: estimate NFL scoring-event antipersistence q = P(same team scores next | lead L) = 1/2 + a - bL from nflverse play-by-play, then simulate rest-of-game scoring events as P(next score by A) = I_A - c_1*r - c_2*Delta with I_A from GSE's pregame rating to produce live win probability plus live spread/total distributions.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Change:** Add an NFL in-play SDE model (X(t) = score differential minus required pace differential, team-pair OU parameters fit from 2010-2024 play-by-play, closed-form P(win|t)) with a discrete-shock layer that perturbs drift on turnovers/injuries with relaxation, as a physics-based alternative to the ML in-play model; use implied sigma as a totals-modeling volatility feature.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Change:** Build an async offseason HPO service: N workers pull (config, fidelity) tasks from a queue (fidelity = training seasons 2 -> 4 -> 8 -> full), joint GP (or CQR surrogate) over (config, seasons), bracket sampling per P(s), fantasize pending evaluations -- async because model families have heterogeneous runtimes (CatBoost fast, FT-Transformer slow).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Change:** Build gse.scores.BivariatePoissonHA: per-season NFL fit -- (home points, away points) ~ BP with log lambda_1 = mu_s + T_s + alpha_H + delta_A, log lambda_2 = mu_s + alpha_A + delta_H; team attack/defense random effects; T_s = season home advantage; extensions: (a) within-season time-varying strengths (state-space); (b) lambda_3 estimated not fixed; (c) COVID-2020 season as T'_2020 with posterior P(decline) -- direct replication of the paper's natural experiment on NFL data; use posterior attack/defense strengths as features for spread/total models.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Change:** Build the joint-distribution staking policy (SinkhornDRL): weekly state from logged picks/odds, action = stake grid, critic outputs N=32 samples of the 3-dim return vector (settled profit, -max intra-week drawdown, mean CLV) with Sinkhorn divergence to the vector Bellman target; scalarize at decision time with a tunable risk price (e.g., maximize E[profit] - 2*E[drawdown] + 0.5*E[CLV]) — then learn the risk price itself as a contextual bandit over the season (meta-action from bankroll state, trained to end-of-season Sharpe).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Change:** Build a between-online changepoint monitor over weekly player series (EPA/play, snap share, NGS top speed/acceleration, target share): segment-specific latent trend + week-specific disturbance (game script, opponent), linear-Gaussian state space + online EM; alert when P(changepoint) > delta -> prop-model flag + feature freeze until the new segment has >=3 weeks (delta tuned for high sensitivity — missing an injury is worse than a false flag); second use = team-level regime detection on offensive EPA/play to trigger model refits; then make the changepoint prior covariate-dependent lambda(X) (injury history, age, snap load, days rest) and allow game-script covariates to modulate week-specific states.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Gate:** ADOPT into the GSE totals pipeline if CMP-SAS beats the Poisson-Maher baseline on out-of-sample IGN for totals in >=2 of 3 seasons AND identifies >=3 teams/season with P(Z_i=1)>0.5 (dispersion heterogeneity exists in NFL scoring); REJECT if no team crosses the 0.5 threshold in any season or IGN gains vanish.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Change:** Adapt the three-step recipe to NFL NGS tracking: functional encoding of route trajectories (polynomial/spline coefficients) + QB/receiver/defender positions -> generative trajectory model -> condition on observed positions -> outcome model (GAM/GBM) mapping encodings to EPA/success (EPV_t = E[positive EPA | tracking state X_t]); derive Decision IQ (QB read quality, marginalized over execution), Execution+ (receiver catch-point value), and Coverage VACC (defender value denied).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Change:** Build a season-episode trajectory dataset for staking: one 'episode' = one NFL season of weekly slates; per week t: R-hat_t = remaining season profit target in units, s_t = slate features (edges, CLV, bankroll, week number, exposure used), a_t = stake-bucket vector (discrete 0/0.25/0.5/1/2u per bet, padded); train a small GPT (4-6 layers, 18-week or K=8 context) with CE loss on stake tokens conditioned on R-hat_1 = +30u season target; each Tuesday prompt with the remaining target and recent (R-hat, s, a) history to emit the week's stake vector — then extend to distributional conditioning: quantile targets (e.g., 'achieve >=+20u with P(drawdown>10u) <= 0.1') as additional conditioning tokens with a quantile-weighted loss.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
