{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Change:** Add the drawdown-modulated governor as bankroll safety infrastructure (not the staking objective): define bankroll drawdown d(k) = 1 - V(k)/max_{j<=k} V(j); set dmax (e.g. 0.20 of bankroll); scale every posted stake by M(k) = (dmax - d(k))/(1 - d(k)) each slate; tune gamma (the Kelly-fraction multiplier) by Monte Carlo over GSE's historical pick returns; add a floor: if d(k) >= dmax, stakes go to zero until recovery -- the automatic drawdown governor that fires when the 1627/1629 circuit-breaker thresholds trip, so no regime can silently eat the bankroll.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports-wt-engineplan/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Change:** Build the double-score no-bet gate: score_A = misclassification detector (calibrated P(engine's pick is wrong | features) from a meta-model on past engine errors); score_B = OOD discriminator (distance of the game's feature vector from the training distribution - Mahalanobis / kNN distance in feature space, or isolation-forest score); no-bet rule: skip if a*score_A + b*score_B > tau, with (a, b, tau) tuned on 2024 - learning the (a,b) weights by direct optimization of selective risk at target coverage (fit the linear combination as a 2-parameter logistic model on past engine outcomes) rather than hand-tuning, and testing the variance estimate as a third score (triple-score).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9101}
